    "text": "Artio was a goddess of wilderness and wildlife. People in Britain and Gaul worshiped her in the form of a bear. Her name Dea Artio means bear. The name Andarta also appears in inscriptions in both lands. These inscriptions appear in Switzerland and in France. Berne means bear city in Switzerland. The second syllable of Andarta links to a bear. In function Artio matches the Greek goddess Artemis. People also saw Artemis as a bear. A bear god named Artaios appears in some regions.",
